[] o  Terminal Rust
[]    How about a probabilistic solution?  Have a chance that items of -3 and
[]    worse fall apart in rusting attacks, just like +N items can melt on
[]    enchantment.  If bathing in a rust trap is considered to be an unfair
[]    exploitation of this rust-to-dust feature, have rust traps dry up--- 
[]    after all they are usually only a problem once.  I thoroughly agree with
[]    the poster who said this gives a much needed reason not to genocide
[]    rust monsters.

i have to admit that when this first surfaced i thought the poster was
whining (forgive me) because his greatest-game-ever just took a turn for
the worse because of some armor-related catastrophe.  i now find that i'm
intrigued by the direction that this is going, fascinating ... i'd like to
see more discussion of features/problems.  how do you deal with rustproof
armor?  can you preemptively apply rust-resistance in preparation for a
rusting attack?  can you over-apply rust-resistance (hence goodbye armor)?
what about non-rusting attacks (i.e. pudding bites)?  should gelatinous
cubes wield long swords???  umm, strike the last thought ...

